---
const choices = [
  {
    name: "WordPress",
    orso: "Your site is already built with Astro, and you want to edit its Markdown content without moving it into WordPress.",
    other: "Choose WordPress for its extensive plugin ecosystem and traditional publishing tools.",
  },
  {
    name: "Wix, Framer, or Webflow",
    orso: "You want a friendly editing workflow while keeping your existing site and deployment outside a visual website platform.",
    other: "Choose a visual builder when you want to design and host the whole site there.",
  },
  {
    name: "Builder.io",
    orso: "You want a focused local workspace and a CMS that writes directly to your Astro content files.",
    other: "Choose Builder.io for a broader visual content and development platform.",
  },
];
---

<section class="border-t border-section-line" id="why-orso">
  <div class="mx-auto max-w-6xl px-6 py-section sm:px-8 sm:py-section-wide">
    <p class="mb-6 text-xs font-medium uppercase tracking-[0.2em] text-brand-accent">Where Orso fits</p>
    <h2 class="max-w-3xl text-4xl font-normal leading-[1.08] tracking-tight text-balance sm:text-5xl lg:text-6xl">Built for the site<br /><span class="text-brand-muted">you keep in GitHub.</span></h2>
    <p class="mt-7 max-w-2xl text-lg leading-relaxed text-brand-muted">
      Orso is for teams that have an Astro site and want a friendlier way to keep it current. The CMS updates the Markdown files in your configured content collections. The agent helps with changes beyond content. Your site stays in your repository and follows your deployment workflow.
    </p>
    <div class="mt-14 grid gap-5 sm:mt-16 lg:grid-cols-3">
      {choices.map((choice) => (
        <article class="flex flex-col rounded-2xl border border-section-line bg-linear-to-b from-section-panel/60 to-section-ink p-6 sm:p-7">
          <h3 class="text-xl font-medium tracking-tight">{choice.name}</h3>
          <p class="mt-7 text-xs font-medium uppercase tracking-[0.16em] text-brand-accent">Choose Orso when</p>
          <p class="mt-3 flex-1 leading-relaxed text-neutral-300">{choice.orso}</p>
          <p class="mt-6 border-t border-section-line pt-6 text-sm leading-relaxed text-brand-muted">{choice.other}</p>
        </article>
      ))}
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
